#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162855} :activity/id #uuid "22c8da45-56d1-5645-85df-aa94cccb29d8" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049855 :topic/id #uuid "1887f465-a1b8-5370-82f6-80e02b9d153a" :topic/math-academy-id 3120} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162855 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163230 :tutorial/content "Suppose that $A$ is an $n\\times n$ symmetric matrix over $\\mathbb{R}.$ The **spectral theorem** states the following:\n\n- The eigenvalues of $A$ are all real.\n- The eigenvectors corresponding to *different* eigenvalues are orthogonal.\n- The dimension of the eigenspace for each eigenvalue equals the multiplicity of that eigenvalue as a root of the characteristic polynomial.\n- $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable." :tutorial/id #uuid "5ecbbdd0-25a0-52ee-8f0c-987dcd8ba584" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4882 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "84b2f14e-f6c7-5b6c-b6d7-19d4d7d71f71" :step/math-academy-id 30533 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162908}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162908 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162019 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161811 :question/id #uuid "6ae71f41-133f-50b6-a286-20ae7e2c3a9d" :question/math-academy-id "e-8291"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c67d532-acd9-5231-a27f-d39084863e01" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048499}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162651} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162665} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365058} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366642} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366649} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366656} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366663}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Spectral Theorem"} :step/id #uuid "95f72e96-f84b-5b21-a070-253638be57a8" :step/math-academy-id 30970 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162909}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162909 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163249 :tutorial/content "We can write an $n\\times n$ symmetric matrix $A$ in terms of a sum of products of its eigenvalues and eigenvectors.\n\nSpecifically, if $\\mathbf{u}_i$ denotes an orthonormal eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda_i$ for $i=1,\\ldots, n$, then\n\n$$A=\\sum_{i=1}^n \\lambda_i \\mathbf{u}_i \\mathbf{u}_i^T.$$\n\nExpressing a symmetric matrix $A$ in this way is called the **spectral decomposition** of $A.$\n\nTo demonstrate, let's find the spectral decomposition of the $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$A = [\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}].$$\n\nThe eigenvalues of $A$ are $\\lambda_1 = 6$ and $\\lambda_2 = -4,$ and the corresponding eigenvectors are\n\n$$\\mathbf{v}_1 = [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\quad \\textrm{and} \\quad \\mathbf{v}_2 = [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$$\n\nThe spectral decomposition of $A$ is given by\n\n$$A =\\sum_{i=1}^2 \\lambda_i \\mathbf{u}_i \\mathbf{u}_i^T = \\lambda_1 \\mathbf u_1 \\mathbf u_1^T + \\lambda_2 \\mathbf u_2 \\mathbf u_2^T,$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf u_1$ and $\\mathbf u_2$ are orthonormal eigenvectors of $A$ corresponding to $\\lambda_1$ and $\\lambda_2,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, let's normalize our eigenvectors:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}_{2} & =\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}$$\n\nTherefore, the spectral decomposition of $A$ is\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}{u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}{u}_{2}^{T} \\\\ & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3\\end{aligned}]+(-4)\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3\\end{aligned}]+(-4)\\cdot \\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ & ={{6}_{⏟}}_{{\\lambda }_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{10} & \\frac{3}{10} \\\\ \\frac{3}{10} & \\frac{9}{10}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{u}_{1}{u}_{1}^{T}}+{{(-4)}_{⏟}}_{{\\lambda }_{2}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{10} & -\\frac{3}{10} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{10} & \\frac{1}{10}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{u}_{2}{u}_{2}^{T}}.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nIn this decomposition, the matrix $\\mathbf{u}_i \\mathbf{u}_i^T$ is the orthogonal projection matrix that maps any $\\mathbf x \\in \\mathbb R^2$ onto the subspace spanned by $\\mathbf u_i.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "a90957e3-e4b9-548d-930b-e060c6b63859" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4973 :tutorial/title "The Spectral Decomposition of a Symmetric Matrix"} :step/id #uuid "8df507ec-4d53-59f1-b941-07907cd14b6f" :step/math-academy-id 30971 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162911}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162910 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162020 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161812 :question/id #uuid "d185ef42-c177-5217-99b7-b42d800f3385" :question/math-academy-id "e-8292"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84207049-12f7-514c-bfa2-51bce8631b41" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049495}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162652} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162668} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365065} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366676} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366683} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378064} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395044} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395051} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395058}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Projection Matrix That Orthogonally Projects a Vector to the Subspace Spanned by an Eigenvector"} :step/id #uuid "2a1d5d86-333c-5361-87ec-fd7766797988" :step/math-academy-id 30972} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162911 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162021 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161813 :question/id #uuid "65b23c21-528f-5df7-a00c-8e2dce041276" :question/math-academy-id "e-8293"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "785b09aa-1b82-5021-8b10-271a063cb916" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162653} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162671} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366690} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375964} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378071} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395065} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395072} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395079}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Spectral Decomposition of a Symmetric Matrix"} :step/id #uuid "86248bdd-6a75-54cd-8196-8b333a64cac5" :step/math-academy-id 30973 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162910}}] :activity/title "The Spectral Theorem" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186162222}]}
